        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R49 0.47; R56 0.47; R6 0.47 (Peristaltic Pump Drivers sheet)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "current-reference divider (/5V_pH, /5V_NA, /5V_NB nets feeding VREF-setting resistors R24–R29)"}
      ],
      "impact": "VREF is near 0 V, so the TMC2209 current setting is near zero; the peristaltic pumps will not run.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["M6B", "U7"],
      "pins": ["M6B.3V3", "U7.VO"],
      "nets": ["+3V3"],
      "observed": "The ESP32-C6-DevKit power unit M6B has its 3V3 pin wired to the board +3V3 rail, which is also driven by the AZ1117-3.3 LDO U7 VO.",
      "expected": "The DevKit should be powered from +5V via its 5V0 pin; its 3V3 output should not be tied to the board's +3V3 rail when U7 is also driving that rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "M6B ESP32-C6-DEVKIT: 5V0 to +5V, 3V3 to +3V3 (Power Train sheet)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U2 — AZ1117-3.3 ... VO feeds +3V3, which powers the I2C pull-ups, isolator primary sides, and TMC2209 logic"}
      ],
      "impact": "Two 3.3 V regulators (DevKit onboard and U7) are connected in parallel, causing regulator conflict, possible overheating, and an unstable +3V3 rail.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T3"],
      "pins": ["T3.G", "T3.D", "T3.S"],
      "nets": ["ATO_VALVE"],
      "observed": "The ATO valve low-side switch T3 is marked AO3400A (SOT-23 N-MOSFET).",
      "expected": "The specification calls for T3 to be an AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) for the ATO solenoid valve.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "T3 AO3400A (Main Pump & Valve Drivers sheet)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch"}
      ],
      "impact": "The AO3400A has a lower current rating and different footprint than the intended AON6407; it may overheat or fail driving the valve, and the PCB footprint may not match.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains several deviations from the intended design: the TMC2209 VREF dividers use 0.47 Ω instead of 0.47 kΩ, the ESP32 DevKit 3V3 output is tied to the board +3V3 LDO output, and the ATO valve MOSFET is an AO3400A instead of the specified AON6407."
}

